cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Aimpoint: open-source environments for beneficial AI capabilities"
message: "If you use Aimpoint, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Aayush
    family-names: Gandhi
    email: aaygan29@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-4649-0367"
    affiliation: "The Sapient Company"
repository-code: "https://github.com/aaygan29/aimpoint"
abstract: >-
  Aimpoint builds open-source RL environments and evaluations for the capabilities we want
  frontier AI to have, rather than only the ones we fear. It enforces three properties the
  harness checks rather than recommends: headline scores computed without an LLM judge,
  mandatory floor and reference baselines, and an explicit defensive-asymmetry argument for
  why competence in each environment does not transfer to harm. Cross-cutting probes measure
  sycophancy, calibrated abstention, fabrication, and behaviour under distribution shift, and
  each environment ships a deliberately flawed proxy metric so specification gaming can be
  measured directly.
keywords:
  - ai-safety
  - evaluation
  - reinforcement-learning
  - beneficial-ai
license: Apache-2.0
